{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00015",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 3.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Hi, nice to see you. Sit down, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.42,
      "end_seconds": 7.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Good morning, uh, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 8.99,
      "end_seconds": 12.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.63,
      "end_seconds": 15.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Did you find the place alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.48,
      "end_seconds": 21.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Yes, it was easy enough. The parking was the hard part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.54,
      "end_seconds": 24.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "So, what's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.0,
      "end_seconds": 29.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "So, I've been passing out once last week, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.6,
      "end_seconds": 31.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.93,
      "end_seconds": 34.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "It happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.56,
      "end_seconds": 38.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.84,
      "end_seconds": 57.75,
      "duration_seconds": 17.91,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a bit of lightheadedness since then as well. The bit of lightheadedness since then? That's been for five days. I've also had a bump on my head after. And I've been feeling hot and sweaty before it as well, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.96,
      "end_seconds": 71.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.3,
      "end_seconds": 73.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.5,
      "end_seconds": 79.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Any loss of bladder control, shaking or jerking or confusion afterwards at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.75,
      "end_seconds": 85.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "No, no loss of bladder control, shaking or jerking or confusion afterwards."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.52,
      "end_seconds": 87.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.81,
      "end_seconds": 89.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Not at all, no palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 90.76,
      "end_seconds": 94.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice palpitations. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.21,
      "end_seconds": 101.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Hmm, um, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.72,
      "end_seconds": 107.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.33,
      "end_seconds": 111.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "So, uh, no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.62,
      "end_seconds": 114.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.19,
      "end_seconds": 119.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "No, you know, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.53,
      "end_seconds": 127.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.52,
      "end_seconds": 139.93,
      "duration_seconds": 12.41,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Yes, an enlarged prostate. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.87,
      "end_seconds": 148.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know. Alright, any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.1,
      "end_seconds": 151.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.34,
      "end_seconds": 156.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.58,
      "end_seconds": 162.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack. Right, my uncle had colon cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.41,
      "end_seconds": 164.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.87,
      "end_seconds": 175.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "Um, yes, I had a lump removed from my back, years ago. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.73,
      "end_seconds": 177.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.56,
      "end_seconds": 182.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.11,
      "end_seconds": 184.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.85,
      "end_seconds": 192.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.0,
      "end_seconds": 199.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 199.87,
      "end_seconds": 207.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "He is on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.86,
      "end_seconds": 212.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I was on telmisartan before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.27,
      "end_seconds": 216.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.75,
      "end_seconds": 227.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Right, carry on. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.73,
      "end_seconds": 240.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.36,
      "end_seconds": 269.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 64 beats a minute, respiratory rate 16, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. And blood pressure 114 over 72, temp 36.8 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.23,
      "end_seconds": 275.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Alright, I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.54,
      "end_seconds": 279.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.04,
      "end_seconds": 299.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "No murmurs on listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.16,
      "end_seconds": 303.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.7,
      "end_seconds": 321.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and there's a small bruise on the right side of the head."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.6,
      "end_seconds": 345.07,
      "duration_seconds": 18.47,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with a simple faint, probably reflex-related. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a heart rhythm problem, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.54,
      "end_seconds": 348.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.24,
      "end_seconds": 367.35,
      "duration_seconds": 18.11,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a simple faint, probably reflex-related, and we'll know more once the a Holter monitor is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been passing out once last week, and no shaking or jerking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.84,
      "end_seconds": 370.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.55,
      "end_seconds": 382.81,
      "duration_seconds": 12.26,
      "text": "Let's get a Holter monitor, for syncope. I'm going to order an ECG, for syncope. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. We should do an echocardiogram for syncope."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.26,
      "end_seconds": 385.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Yeah, alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.09,
      "end_seconds": 410.7,
      "duration_seconds": 23.61,
      "text": "Drink enough water and avoid standing still for long stretches, and sit if you feel it coming. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. If you pass out again, especially with chest pain or palpitations, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.66,
      "end_seconds": 413.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.77,
      "end_seconds": 425.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "Let's review you in two weeks. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.2,
      "end_seconds": 433.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "So, I come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.4,
      "end_seconds": 439.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.08,
      "end_seconds": 443.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "So, nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.43,
      "end_seconds": 445.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}